00:27:41.390 --> 00:27:42.390
But that's a good thing.

00:27:42.390 --> 00:27:44.470
Because we can't
visualize it yet.

00:27:44.470 --> 00:27:49.950
So if we were to use that
Kubernetes dashboard and wanted

00:27:49.950 --> 00:27:54.810
to visualize a low workload
that is running in 10 Kubernetes

00:27:54.810 --> 00:27:57.420
clusters, what are
we going to do?

00:27:57.420 --> 00:27:59.550
Install it in each
